*Infinite [[Malevolent Lion Cat]]s spawn after 366.67 seconds<sup>11,000f</sup>, delay 46.67~53.33 seconds<sup>1,400f~1,600f</sup>.

==Strategy==
With a combination of five extremely hard-pushing Malevolent Cats and J.J. Jackrabbit on the side with Sir Seals being your only money source, this stage is INSANELY hard without proper preparation and even good [[:Category:Uber Rare Cats|Uber]]/[[:Category:Legend Rare Cats|Legend Rares]] to carry you through it. Malevolent Mohawk comes up first rushing to your base and constantly being juggled by attacks, Malevolent Lions come out to push through easily thanks to their low knockback counts and [[Shield]]s, Malevolent Dark constantly assaults your cats and can even Curse them, Malevolent Flying stays at the back, nuking anyone who gets into its range and worst of all, Malevolent Jamiera, turns Heinous Road into a luck-based mission with his Savage Blow, often being the reason you lose to this stage in the first place. If you even think about bringing [[:Category:Surge Attack Cats|units that create Surge Attacks]], remember that Malevolent Jamiera's [[Counter-Surge]] can also Savage Blow, killing nearly anything that walks into it, including [[Maize Cat (Rare Cat)|Cone Cat]]. While this stage IS scary, it is very well possible with enough luck and good units.

It is recommended that your units are at '''LEAST''' level 50+ for this stage, as they will not survive for long enough if they are any weaker.

==='''Recommended Units'''===
*[[Maize Cat (Rare Cat)|Cone Cat]]: An absolute powerhouse of a meatshield that can tank nearly every single enemy in this stage, albeit synergizes poorly with Surge units.
*[[Ancient Egg: N003 (Special Cat)|Cat Cactus]]: This meatshield is less effective than Cone Cat and prone to getting cursed by Malevolent Dark, but has Surge Immunity.
*[[Brainwashed Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Brainwashed Mohawk Cat]]: Cheap, spammable and can become invincible for a short amount of time with some luck. Just watch out for Sir Seal and J.J. Jackrabbit.
*[[Talents|Talented]] [[Matador Cat (Rare Cat)|Bellydance Cat]]: Albeit the least consistent of the four [[:Category:Anti-Aku Cats|anti-Aku]] specialist meatshields mentioned, if you're lucky enough, this unit can change the tides of battle quickly, and unlike Brainwashed Mohawk, Bellydance actually has some bulk and can dodge Sir Seal, Ginger Snache and J.J. Jackrabbit.
*[[Stone Cat (Rare Cat)|Boulder Cat]]: Can stall the enemies up front for a short amount of time, and can even survive being Savage Blowed by Malevolent Jamiera.
*[[Ancient Egg: N101 (Rare Cat)|Courier Cat]]: Can snipe the [[:Category:Red Enemies|Red]] peons and chip through Malevolent Mohawk.
*[[Sniper the Recruit (Super Rare Cat)|Sniper the Deadeye]]: Great for the Malevolent Jamiera phase, being able to prevent him from pushing thanks to KB + Slow, and pairs well with [[Summoner Satoru (Uber Rare Cat)|Summoner Satoru]]. Just don't let him get distracted by oncoming peons due to his single target.
*[[Nerd Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Cyberpunk Cat]]: Synergizes VERY well with Sniper the Deadeye, able to slow enemies from an extremely long distance while sniper knocks them back. Of course, with a sizable blind spot, meatshielding is going to be very important to make sure he lands his hits, but if used properly and stacked, he will be able to permaslow the Malevolent Cats when their Shields are down.
*[[Nymph Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Fiend Cat]]: Essentially Sniper the Deadeye, but is more spammable and has Area Attack. With his 30% chance to knockback Aku enemies, Fiend will be able to effectively crowd-control the Malevolents (save for Malevolent Mohawk).
*[[Aku Researcher (Rare Cat)|Cat Researcher]] and [[Ancient Egg: N109 (Rare Cat)|Barrel Cat]]: Essential for this stage, their consistent Shield Piercing abilities are almost required for this stage due to every Malevolent here having a decently durable Shield. Their Shield Piercing still isn't guaranteed, however, so using both at the same time would be very effective here.
*[[Vaulter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Housewife Cat]]: One of your main sources of damage on this stage, especially with her Savage Blow Talent. Being spammable and fairly inexpensive, she will not drain your cash while being able to provide a decent amount of damage to chip away at the enemies.
*[[Paperboy Cat (Rare Cat)|Paperboy Cat]]: With Insane Damage vs Aku, great speed, and being fairly spammable, this unit is an absolute monster and an exceptional option for nuking Malevolent Mohawk and the Malevolent Lions, and even good for chipping Malevolent Dark with the use of stepping stones. You will, however, need to beat [[Feathergeddon: Swan Song (Brutal)|Feathergeddon]] first.

==='''Recommended Ubers'''===
*[[Summoner Satoru (Uber Rare Cat)|Devil Hunter Satoru]]: Having 50% chance to pierce shields as well as 100% chance to knockback and slow Aku for six seconds, Satoru can greatly impede most of the Malevolent Cats here, though Malevolent Mohawk has to be tackled with other units as it is Immune to Knockback and Slow. His LD enables him to reach even Malevolent Flying, and knocking the Aku threats behind the base can potentially allow other LD units to cheese the stage. Just be wary that he is very frail and his high speed may result in him clipping into Malevolent Flying's range (640 > 470).
*[[Hajime Saito (Uber Rare Cat)|Hajime Saito]]: Really powerful rusher against all enemies here, especially against Malevolent Mohawk, where if he is timed well, he can chain-knockback Malevolent Mohawk as long as the frontline doesn't have a major shift in positioning. He's also able to pierce through Malevolent Flying's Shield effectively. Be careful with him, however, as he has poor stamina like most rushers and lacks immunities, making him risky to use against Malevolent Dark who can curse him.
* [[Bunny & Canard (Uber Rare Cat)| Malevolent Mad Duck]]: A great attacker for this stage being able to attack all enemies with huge damage although beware that this unit cannot outrange Malevolent Flying along with its high cost which could drain your resources and long cooldown time.
*[[Mighty Deth-Troy-R (Uber Rare Cat)|Obliterator Diabolosa]]: Very high damage against Aku. Though lacking in most immunities, it has enough range to be safe from a majority of the threats here, and its slow speed is beneficial to prevent it from running into Malevolent Flying's range quickly. If you can spare a slot for [[Crazed Bird Cat (Super Rare Cat)| Manic Flying]] it will grant you a 15% attack up combo which will massively help other attackers.
*[[Ultra Talents|Ultra Talented]] [[Takeda Shingen (Uber Rare Cat)|Immortal Shingen]]: Similar to Obliterator Diabolosa, but with MUCH higher stats.
*[[Child of Destiny Phono (Uber Rare Cat)|King of Destiny Phonoa]]: Very high range and high damage against everything in this stage, quickly tearing through every threat with ease.
*[[Kaoru Hanayama (Uber Rare Cat)|Kaoru Hanayama]]: Being Resistant to Aku threats with Massive Damage to them as well as Immunity to a wide variety of status effects (most notably Malevolent Dark Cat's Curse), Hanayama reaches nearly a million HP with 650K damage per hit at level 50 against Aku, topped by guaranteed shield piercing. His single knockback enables him to tank the Aku threats long enough for him to gravely cripple them if not kill them outright, and his long foreswing gives enemies enough time to walk into his range. (Assuming he is not boosted by Attack Up combos, he can kill Mohawk in 6 hits, Dark in 4, Lion in 1, Flying in 2 and Jamiera in 4). Just make sure to keep him somewhat protected and avoid surge attackers (though using them may not be necessary), while he slaughters everything.
*Ultra Talented [[Kai (Uber Rare Cat)|Divine Kai μ]]: Sporting INSANELY high health and damage, guaranteed Shield Piercing and a low cooldown, she is very potent at tanking and dealing damage, despite the amount of damage Malevolent Jamiera can output; if she's close to dying, she can be easily replaced. If her Ultra Talents are unlocked, she can even directly tank the Aku threats due to targeting them.
*[[King of Doom Phono (Uber Rare Cat)|King of Extinction Phono]]: God-like range and crowd-control ability. Although, be careful of their [[Mini-Surge]]s, which could and most likely will activate several Counter-Surges from the Malevolent Cats. However, the Mini-Surges only carry 20% of their original damage (unless Malevolent Jamiera Savage Blows), so that would not be very threatening to your non-Surge-immune units, besides Sniper the Deadeye and Cyberpunk.
*[[Daybreaker Izanagi (Legend Rare Cat)|Dawnbringer Izanagi]]: With insane damage vs traited, a three-part multi-hit that extends far beyond his standing range, and high DPS only rivaled by that of a level 60 [[Lesser Demon Cat (Uber Rare Cat)|Greater Balrog Cat]] if at level 50, Izanagi proves to be an extremely useful asset. His high health allows him to survive multiple hits (and even a Savage Blow from Malevolent Jamiera at level 50!), and ridiculous DPS can absolute shred all of the Malevolents as long as their shields are down. His lack of Surge Immunity should not be a concern, as Surge units should not be brought alongside him here.
*Ultra Talented [[Hayabusa (Uber Rare Cat)|Akuma Hayabusa]]: If you have proper meatshields, Hayabusa, even if he is your lone attacker, can absolutely shred through the Villainous Gods, with his new doubled attack speed deleting shields and activating procs incredibly fast. The only true consistent threat to Hayabusa's safety when guarded in this level is [[Malevolent Jamiera Cat]], as his Omnistrike might pierce through the meatshields. Keep in mind that every Talent and Ultra Talent MUST be unlocked.

